# __PACKAGE__ implementation checklist

This package is a **non-running skeleton**, not a consensus algorithm. Constructors
and every protocol transition reject use with `ErrNotImplemented`. The example
wire header and runtime plumbing do not supply a commit rule, quorum, recovery
algorithm, or client routing policy. Do not remove the startup guard until the
design and the implementation below agree.

| File | Fill in from the finalized design |
| --- | --- |
| `defs.go` | Commands, messages, identities, ballots, evidence, output types. |
| `wire.go` | Factories and encoding for every message, with bounded allocations. |
| `core.go` | Local state, Propose/Handle/Tick, unique voters, normal commit rule. |
| `recovery.go` | Evidence collection, safe selection, fallback, missing-data repair. |
| `execute.go` | Executable order, deduplication, result retention, client completion. |
| `replica.go` | Configuration validation, stable replica IDs, callback setup, RPC registration. |
| `plan.go` | Initial leader/quorum/responder/ingress policy from deployment inputs, including fixed policies. |
| `runtime.go` | Serialized event delivery, explicit time, output dispatch, observability. |
| `transport.go` | Ownership of queued data, queue bounds, failure/retry policy, self-delivery. |
| `client.go` | Ingress choice, routing, and exact completion evidence. |

`Replica` implements the shared `protocol.Machine` event interface through
`Propose(*defs.GPropose, time.Time) error`, `Handle(any, time.Time) error`, and
`Tick(protocol.Tick) error`. Its live loop uses these methods. The core's private
`effects` are dispatched inside the method; they are not a framework-wide output
barrier. Match the ownership and timer rules in `protocol/README.md` at the
repository root when replacing the guards.

The fixed-header codec is only an example; extend it with the message definition.
Transport currently rejects self-delivery and exits its event loop on queue errors;
choose retry policies before enabling
the implementation. The membership check and `(n-1)/2` framework argument are not
a substitute for the design's fault/quorum validation. Persistence, restart,
reconnect, and complete process shutdown are not implemented by this skeleton;
its runtime does close registered senders when the event loop exits.

Keep the protocol's state transitions free of sockets, goroutines, and wall-clock
reads. Feed time into transitions and execute every transition on one event loop.
The `execute` hook applies a state-machine command; the core must establish the
required execution condition before invoking it. `effects.Replies` means the
protocol has authorized client completion, not merely received a proposal.

Run `go build ./__PACKAGE__` and `go vet -composites=false ./__PACKAGE__` after
generating into the default directory. Add one entry and an import in the root
`protocols.go` when implementation is ready; see `templates/README.md` for the
integration contract. Registration is intentionally not performed by the generator.
